␀
␀Integers are signed 1024-bit values.
␀Operators:
␀  +   add
␀  -   subtract or unary negation
␀  +   unary plus
␀  *   multiply
␀  /   divide
␀  //  integer division (integers only)
␀  %%   modulus (integers only)
␀  ^   power (exponent)
␀  ~   unary bitwise not (integers only)
␀  =   equality comparison
␀  parentheses: ( and )
␀Examples:
␀  2 + 2          -> 4
␀  10.0 / 4       -> 2.5
␀  10 // 4        -> 2
␀  (3 + 5) * 2    -> 16
␀  7 %% 3          -> 1
␀  2 ^ 3          -> 8
␀  ~5             -> -6
␀  -5 + 3         -> -2
␀ ␀/help␀Error: %s
